    description: "Found during the WI-zulij validation re-probe (2026-08-01, dev 529e4aebe3). Verified in source.\n\ncompact.py has three selection/format entry points and they DISAGREE about whether the canonical\nis_excluded_kind predicate applies:\n\n  compact.py:1421  select_by_tokens            -- applies it\n  compact.py:1720  format_tiered_behavior_map  -- applies it\n  compact.py:890-1357  select_by_coverage      -- DOES NOT. This is the DEFAULT compact path.\n\nVerified: grep for is_excluded_kind in compact.py returns exactly four hits -- the docstring at\n:40, the import at :87, and the two call sites at :1421 and :1720. There is no call inside\nselect_by_coverage's line range.\n\nMEASURED CONSEQUENCE (from the WI-zulij probe, independently reproduced by a second agent using\nthe imported predicate rather than a hand-rolled set): at --max-symbols 10 across the eight 07-17\nbakeoff maps, 17 of 80 emitted nodes are kinds the predicate rejects -- file 14, variable 2,\npackage 1. \"file\" is in EXCLUDED_KINDS in selection/filters.py. The two agents' K=100 numbers\ndisagree on the denominator because one run used an inconsistent --min-symbols, so treat the\nK=10 figure as the sound one and re-measure K=100 before citing it.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND TIDINESS: the excluded kinds are excluded precisely because they have high\ncentrality without representing useful code, so leaking them into the default path's ranked\noutput puts noise at the top of what the tool advertises as its most important symbols. On the\n07-17 maps the leading emitted nodes include run*.sh and install.sh shell files and a\ncompletions script -- i.e. the noise is not evenly distributed, it concentrates at the head.\n\nRELATIONSHIP TO WI-batit: this is plausibly a partial root cause of the ordering/noise face\ntracked there, since the leading noise nodes measured are precisely EXCLUDED_KINDS members that\nthe default path never filters. Confirm rather than assume -- WI-batit's own framing is about\nseed ranking, and the seeds are force-included ahead of the ranked fill by a separate mechanism\n(compact.py:1247), so the two can both be contributing.\n\nOpen question the fix has to answer rather than assume: whether select_by_coverage's omission is\nan oversight or a deliberate choice for the coverage-driven path (coverage is computed over the\nfull graph, so filtering kinds mid-selection changes what coverage means). Read the coverage stop\nlogic before adding the call.\n\nNOT tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: no quantitative bakeoff-improvement claim has been made\nyet. Tag at merge time if the fix ships with one."  # 1982
    fields: {}  # 1982
